{
  "id": "22648_rurou",
  "headword": "{流浪|るろう}",
  "reading": "るろう",
  "romaji": "rurou",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "wandering; vagrancy; roaming",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "wandering; vagrancy; roaming",
      "explanation": "Traveling from place to place without a fixed home or destination. Carries a literary or dramatic nuance, often evoking hardship or a rootless existence."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "22648_rurou_ex1",
      "japanese": "{流浪|るろう}の{旅|たび}に{出|で}る。",
      "english": "To set out on a wandering journey.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22648_rurou_ex2",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{何年|なんねん}も{流浪|るろう}の{生活|せいかつ}を{送|おく}った。",
      "english": "He led a wandering life for many years.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22648_rurou_ex3",
      "japanese": "{戦争|せんそう}で{故郷|こきょう}を{失|うしな}った{人々|ひとびと}は{各地|かくち}を{流浪|るろう}するしかなかった。",
      "english": "People who lost their homeland in the war had no choice but to wander from place to place.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A literary term for aimless wandering, often implying hardship or displacement. More dramatic and evocative than everyday words for traveling.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {流浪|るろう}の{民|たみ}: wandering people, nomads\n- {流浪|るろう}の{旅|たび}: a wandering journey\n- {流浪|るろう}の{生活|せいかつ}: a vagabond life\n- {流浪|るろう}する: to wander, to roam\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {放浪|ほうろう}: wandering — very similar but slightly more neutral; often used for voluntary wandering or adventure\n- {漂泊|ひょうはく}: drifting — more literary, emphasizes being carried along without purpose\n- さまよう: to wander — a verb with a sense of being lost or confused\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nFamously used in the manga/anime title {流浪|るろう}に{剣心|けんしん} (Rurouni Kenshin), which popularized the word among younger generations.",
